# Build artefacts.
#
# The snapshot is rebuilt with `python -m harness --build`; committing it would
# put a moving EDGAR extract in version control, and the dataset's expectations
# are resolved from whichever snapshot is in use, so a committed copy would go
# stale against the code that reads it.
#
# The cross-framework archive is the same kind of thing and is ignored for the
# same reason: it is an EDGAR extract for a set of issuers, rebuilt by
# `build_snapshot(..., issuers=..., forms=...)`, and the 2.7 report records the
# numbers it produced. Committing one live archive while ignoring its sibling
# would leave the repository with two different rules for the same artefact
# depending on which phase produced it.
snapshot.sqlite
snapshot.sqlite-*
snapshot-crossframework.sqlite
snapshot-crossframework.sqlite-*

# Source inventories, fetched by `fetch_source_inventory.py`. A moving EDGAR
# extract like the archives above, and gitignored for the same reason: the
# *derived* numbers are committed (in the collection chains, the reports and the
# ledger output) and the responses are reproducible with one command per issuer.
inventory/
inventory/*

# Run outputs. A run of the *sealed* dataset against a real model is the
# evidence this experiment exists to produce, so those are committed; the
# verification runs of scripted targets are noise and are not.
#
#   committed:  runs/ollama-local-*/
#   ignored:    runs/scripted-*/, runs/reference-*/, runs/unknown-*/
snapshot.sqlite
snapshot.sqlite-*

runs/scripted-*/
runs/reference-*/
runs/unknown-*/

__pycache__/
